    "reason": "[ev-efc5158ff817] and [ev-9beeb11a214a] show that refreshPolicy (CreatedOnce/Periodic/OnChange) was added to ExternalSecret and to ClusterExternalSecret's externalSecretSpec. The excerpts cut off before any default appears, so the evidence does not say how an ExternalSecret that leaves the field unset behaves after the upgrade. The PR [ev-998860a436f5][ev-f69689db02ca] says that even with refreshInterval 0, updating labels or annotations can now trigger a refresh. That hints that resources which leave the field unset may behave differently, but it does not say so. Without the default and the unset-field behaviour, I can't tell whether the proposed 'refreshPolicy unset' condition is correct, too broad (if nothing changes, no environment is exposed) or too narrow (it leaves out ClusterExternalSecret and the refreshInterval 0 case).",
